{
 "id": "2026-11-20-florida-st-johns-record-flood",
 "lang": "en",
 "gap": 0.7,
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Florida's longest river just broke a flood record from 1953. What pushed it over?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Over ten inches of rain fell on parts of Broward County in twelve hours on Tuesday, Newsweek reports. Fort Lauderdale, Melbourne and West Palm Beach broke November rainfall records. In Brevard County, the sheriff says crews rescued more than a hundred people on Thursday."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "That water drains into the St. Johns River. Near Cocoa, it rose above eighteen feet on Thursday, local media report, citing weather service data. That beats the record from 1953. The weather service says it will stay above flood stage into next week."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Governor Ron DeSantis has expanded a state of emergency to twenty-one counties and called in the National Guard. Forecasters say the system could become Subtropical Storm Kyle, with rain and coastal flooding up the East Coast."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the St. Johns drop below flood stage by Thanksgiving? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
