  "title": "Florida's St. Johns River Tops Its 1953 Flood Record #shorts",
  "description": "Days of heavy rain flooded Florida's Atlantic coast this week: over ten inches fell on parts of Broward County in twelve hours, and more than a hundred people were rescued in Brevard County on Thursday. The St. Johns River near Cocoa rose above its 1953 record, and Governor DeSantis expanded the state of emergency to 21 counties. Forecasters say the system could become Subtropical Storm Kyle.\n\nSources: Newsweek, CNN, CBS News, Fox Weather, AP (via ABC News), ClickOrlando, Spectrum News 13, CBS12 (based on search-result excerpts). Rain areas on the map are illustrative and the river course is approximate.\n\n#climate #weather #florida #flooding",
